{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109339-could-the-ratkin-destroy-humanity-right-now","id":1109339,"title":"Could the Ratkin destroy humanity right now?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-29T11:54:20-07:00","id":1109339,"title":"Could the Ratkin destroy humanity right now?","content":"Is there any reason that the Ratkin couldn't purge the Earth right now of humans or at least reduce our numbers down to a more appropriate population number?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T12:22:24-07:00","id":1109344,"title":"","content":"Pick one: FEMA, the CDC, the Progenitors, Gaia, the Samedi, the Verbena...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T07:30:13-07:00","id":1109752,"title":"","content":"Yes, but they do not realize it. With modern international transportation and trade, a weaponized version of pneumonic plague that had been made resistant to antibiotics in the laboratory could kill off 50% of humans within a month. The resulting chaos would likely kill off 50% of the survivors of the plague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T07:39:16-07:00","id":1110539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109339-could-the-ratkin-destroy-humanity-right-now?p=1109752#post1109752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but they do not realize it. With modern international transportation and trade, a weaponized version of pneumonic plague that had been made resistant to antibiotics in the laboratory could kill off 50% of humans within a month. The resulting chaos would likely kill off 50% of the survivors of the plague.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would the results be, in regards to Gaia? Would the psychic backlash kill her, or would she at last be saved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T08:26:40-07:00","id":1110552,"title":"","content":"Gaia is far too powerful to be killed by a minor extinction of humans, even in her weakened state, but it would only delay the inevitable given that the human species could replace its numbers in just a century. The only potential positive effect would be that it could buy enough time for humans to change their behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T22:57:16-07:00","id":1111170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109339-could-the-ratkin-destroy-humanity-right-now?p=1110552#post1110552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaia is far too powerful to be killed by a minor extinction of humans, even in her weakened state, but it would only delay the inevitable given that the human species could replace its numbers in just a century. The only potential positive effect would be that it could buy enough time for humans to change their behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>All those souls going to Oblivion is probably going to have a horrible bang on effect for the Earth even if it doesn't effect things directly. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T10:27:15-07:00","id":1111331,"title":"","content":"I do not know. The Earth is not the Creation of Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T17:34:31-07:00","id":1111903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109339-could-the-ratkin-destroy-humanity-right-now?p=1111331#post1111331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not know. The Earth is not the Creation of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Earth in WoD <i>is</i> attached to the Underworld, part of the Umbra, where Great Maelstroms happen, usually caused by massive numbers of human casualties.<br /> <br /> Sidenote: Oblivion is in the Underworld, too. It's... Kind of the driving force of nature(?) there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":".  Wraith exists. 07-05-2017, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T08:35:04-07:00","id":1113258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109339-could-the-ratkin-destroy-humanity-right-now?p=1111331#post1111331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not know. The Earth is not the Creation of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It may not be flat or have five elemental poles but Wraith and Exalted Underworld have ALOT of metaphysical similarities and some locational ones. However Wraith time isn't set by a clock. Assuming vast crossover setup. Ratkin have always been failures. Vast amounts of human death cause maelstroms. Maelstroms explicitly expand Oblivions' reach in the Dark Umbra. While I don't agree that Oblivion is one for one the Wyrm it sure as hell is bad for Gaia.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it Ratkin fundimentally benefit from failure on their part. As humans spread so do their numbers. Their kinfolk numbers have never been greater than they are now. The Destruction of Humanity or at least a strong hit against civilization would ultimately lead to fewer rats. Ultimately Ratkin are really conceptually off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T12:52:47-07:00","id":1113334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109339-could-the-ratkin-destroy-humanity-right-now?p=1113258#post1113258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It may not be flat or have five elemental poles but Wraith and Exalted Underworld have ALOT of metaphysical similarities and some locational ones. However Wraith time isn't set by a clock. Assuming vast crossover setup. Ratkin have always been failures.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they were massacred for trying to do their duty. They've been building up since then, which wasn't easy with everything else trying to kill them, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vast amounts of human death cause maelstroms. Maelstroms explicitly expand Oblivions' reach in the Dark Umbra. While I don't agree that Oblivion is one for one the Wyrm it sure as hell is bad for Gaia. </div> </div> </div>Then salt that shit en masse, if we're going down the &quot;similarities with Exalted&quot; route. Spill salt on ghosts like cheap french fries, and they lose their hold and can't interact with the skinlands quite so easily anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Come to think of it Ratkin fundimentally benefit from failure on their part. As humans spread so do their numbers. Their kinfolk numbers have never been greater than they are now. The Destruction of Humanity or at least a strong hit against civilization would ultimately lead to fewer rats. Ultimately Ratkin are really conceptually off. </div> </div> </div>Most Ratkin are rodens breed. While they still technically do thrive in humanity's shadows, their goal must eventually be met. Given their purpose in life, they probably recognize that it's not good to have quite so many of their own around. That's why they kick out their own version of rabble from established nests, who then often make new nests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T22:30:30-07:00","id":1113599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109339-could-the-ratkin-destroy-humanity-right-now?p=1113334#post1113334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they were massacred for trying to do their duty. They've been building up since then, which wasn't easy with everything else trying to kill them, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that. I'm saying that conceptually the Ratkin are kind of odd. They are incentivized the fail on a level no other breed is. I think its an odd choice on a game design level that their actions should in theory hurt and hinder both breeds to succeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then salt that shit en masse, if we're going down the &quot;similarities with Exalted&quot; route. Spill salt on ghosts like cheap french fries, and they lose their hold and can't interact with the skinlands quite so easily anymore. </div> </div> </div>Um. not an exalted thing. was trying to get across Wraith. Lots of human deaths effects the world. I mean if we care about the Technocracy, or Camarilla or whatever getting involved then &quot;Causes enough deaths to drop the Underworld into Oblivion&quot; is probably a thing that gives the wyrm a stronger grip on reality.<br /> <br /> If we are going more purist the Ratkin come off abit better but still kind of insane.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most Ratkin are rodens breed. While they still technically do thrive in humanity's shadows, their goal must eventually be met. Given their purpose in life, they probably recognize that it's not good to have quite so many of their own around. That's why they kick out their own version of rabble from established nests, who then often make new nests. </div> </div> </div>I get that I just find that on a metalevel they are kind of off. I get the explanation it just seems like an odd choice from a development stance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}